  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YCC The Movements Trust</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The COP30 Media Training Fellowship is a multilingual, multi-partner initiative running from July to November 2025 that equips youth climate leaders with the tools, platforms, and resources to shape the public narrative leading into COP30. Led by Youth Climate Collaborative with core partners including Oxfam, The Carmack Collective, 350.org, Instituto Oya, Econews, and ChilliApp, the Fellowship supports fellows through a mix of online and in-person media training sessions in English, Portuguese, Spanish,and French. Fellows gain access to curated and crowdsourced media opportunities, campaign support, databases of tools and training, and proactive mentorship to pitch op-eds, interviews, and creative content. In-person trainings will take place during Africa Climate Week, New York Climate Week, and COP30 in Bel&#xe9;m, Brazil. Fellows engaged in long-term campaigns may also receive funding support through Chilli App.The program is grounded in a coordinated narrative strategy with key partners to ensure alignedmessaging across the climate movement&#x2014;especially in support of youth, frontline voices, and Brazilian-led efforts like the Mutir&#xe3;o. This effort aims to democratize access to media training and influence, ensuring young, underrepresented voices are not justpresent at COP30, but have the connections toamplify their stories, actively shape core messaging, and influence policy outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
